  "articleBody": "Getting your tiny guest home permitted can feel like a big hurdle, especially with San Diego’s unique local rules. But don't worry, it's definitely doable! The main thing to remember is that the process depends heavily on whether your guest home is on a permanent foundation (like an ADU) or on wheels. If it's a foundation-based ADU, you'll be looking at specific zoning requirements and building codes from either the City of San Diego or the County. For mobile tiny homes, the rules can be different entirely, often falling under personal property classifications. We've got over a decade of experience helping clients navigate these pathways. From understanding the initial property assessment to dealing with the permitting office, we can guide you through every step. Our goal is to make your guest home accessible and affordable, without sacrificing quality or legality. When you’re ready to build your guest home, having an expert on your side makes all the difference in getting those permits approved smoothly.",
